  "body": "### Summary\n\nThe MP list page past the last page is now captured (`R96a`, #114): it is an ordinary empty list page (200, no `.hop`, header row, no topic row, pager 1-7 with \"Page Précédente\" only), not a message page. `PrivateMessageListParser`'s doc says such a page \"may be\" a `.hop` \"never captured\"; it should be tested on `R96a` and the caveat removed.\n\n### Facts\n\n- `R96a`: user1's list, `page=8` of 7, legacy's `MPStorage.m:694` query. `<title>` \"Messages privés - FORUM HardWare.fr - Page : 8\". No current-page marker in the pager.\n- `R95j`: an empty list (no row, no pager) after a thread delete.\n- HFR-PROTOCOL §6b \"MP list past the last page\" (run 9).\n\n### Change\n\n- `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRParsing/Lists/PrivateMessageListParser.swift`: drop the \"past the end after a deletion, never captured\" caveat (a `.notAuthenticated` on the MP list is a login wall on every page); keep callers' behaviour unless a test shows otherwise.\n- Tests (Swift Testing) on `R96a` and `R95j`: zero threads, no throw; assert what `navigation` reports for page 8 of 7 (current page, last page, previous link) and fix the pager reading if it claims a next page or a wrong last page. The LOT-002 oracles `LOT-002/R96a.oracle.json`, `R95j.oracle.json` give legacy's output.\n\nRefs #114\n",
